id: 1778630448636
parent-id: 0
command:  
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
>  


Six years of work, countless hours in the library and the lab, hunched over your
laptop, poring over old manuscripts or departmental paperwork...and now it’s
almost over. Your advisor has given you a deadline, and you need to defend your
thesis by the end of the year, or leave with nothing to show for it.

Your data is promising. The experimental results are fantastic, the p-values are
significant, and you’ve gotten a couple publications out of the process. But
numbers don’t convince people—stories do. If you want to be the first ever PhD
in Forensic Necromancy, you need more than tables and graphs. You need a
narrative, something new and exciting, that will grab public attention and make
the academic establishment listen.

Which means you need human remains in situ, and the older the better. The last
of your advisor’s grant funding got you to Nineveh just after midnight. The rest
is up to you.

[0m[50m             [0m[7m[50m                  [0m[1m[7m[50mA MURDER IN NINEVEH[0m[7m[50m                 [0m[50m             
             [0m[7m[50m Submitted in partial fulfillment of the requirements [0m[50m             
             [0m[7m[50m       for the degree of Doctor of Philosophy in      [0m[50m             
             [0m[7m[50m                  [0m[1m[7m[50mFORENSIC NECROMANCY[0m[7m[50m                 [0m[50m             
