> w
Each memory only captures a brief moment in time: what the person saw, heard,
and felt in those scant few seconds. Everything beyond that is lost in a dark
haze.

If you want to go back to the memory palace, there’s a tear in the haze to the
<southeast>, like a hole crudely ripped in a cloth backdrop.

