> sw
You move toward the traces of motion, and the dream shifts...

[0m[4m“Absolutely not.” You glare across the table at your brother. The single lamp
gives his face a strange, uncanny cast. “We have everything to lose, and [0mnothing[0m[4m
to gain.”

“Except for saving someone’s life. Saving the [0mking’s[0m[4m life!”

“He wasn’t crowned by Marduk. He’s no true king. And have you forgotten what he
did to Babylon? Let the Assyrians all stab each other in the back. What happens
up in Nineveh isn’t our concern.”

“If some Babylonians save the king’s life, maybe that will change.” He searches
your face, eyes gleaming, and sighs at what he sees. “And besides. The crown
prince is different. Asshur-ahu-iddina spends time around here, he fixes things
that need fixing. Urad-Mullissi is just another Assyrian. If he seizes the
throne, this continues on for a generation more. If we stop this, if Asshur-ahu-
iddina inherits, we’ll have someone reasonable in power. Someone who will get
Marduk’s blessing and rebuild the temples.”

You close your eyes for a long moment. “Fine. Make the trip, make your report.
I’ll take care of things back here. But if you expect gratitude from the
Assyrians...”

You meet his gaze and hold it as the shadows start to close in. “You’re going to
be disappointed.”

And the light gutters out.
