You step back into the light.

[0m[1mRoyal palace[0m
The architecture here looks Assyrian—it must be Nineveh, the same place your
body is in the real world. But the <lamassu> are taller than a three-story
building, the ceilings so high they're lost in the clouds. This is Nineveh as
remembered by its enemies, majestic and imposing, larger than life.

Bits and pieces of a dozen rooms meet at odd angles, columns blocking doorways,
hallways slicing through walls. The doorway to the north is grand and richly
decorated, while the one to the east is too dark to see. Southeast, a passage
has intersected a brazier and spilled <no-longer-hot coals> across the floor;
west, an outdoor balcony juts in a meter above the floor.

