> lines
These surveying lines don’t look too different from the cords the modern
archaeologists used to lay out their grid. Even thousands of years later, the
best way to make a straight line is still to stretch a rope between a couple of
pegs. Instead of a regular grid, though, these ones seem to be tracing the
original walls, making sure the new ones follow exactly the same outline.

